<main id="main" data-pagefind-body><section class="reference-intro"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE JOURNAL</p><h1>Stories with a<br><em>reference trail.</em></h1><p>Sanatan Heritage is an illustrated introduction to Sanatan Dharma: its ideas, divine forms, sacred texts and stories. It offers starting points for curious readers and families.</p></section><div class="section editorial-standards">
<section><h2>Our purpose</h2><p>Help readers move from a question to a story, then to its wider textual and devotional setting. The site offers introductory explanations and condensed English retellings, alongside links for further reading.</p></section>
<section><h2>Sources and editions</h2><p>Story cards and readers link to the central <a href="/sources.html">Sources &amp; References</a> page. References name texts, editions and chapter or verse locations where available. A retelling condenses its source; it is not a complete translation. The referenced text remains the place to examine the fuller account.</p><p>Translations and commentaries reflect the perspectives of their authors and traditions. Introductory sources, primary texts and editorial reflections have different roles.</p></section>
<section><h2>Different traditions</h2><p>Hindu traditions preserve many tellings and interpretations. A reader identifies the account it follows rather than silently merging versions. Tradition notes and <a href="/sources.html#different-tellings">comparisons on the Sources page</a> help make these distinctions visible. Reflection questions are editorial invitations, not quotations from scripture.</p></section>
<section><h2>Images and pronunciation</h2><p>Captions identify contributed photographs, devotional artwork and AI-generated illustrations. Illustrations are interpretations of a story or setting; they are not evidence of historical appearance, an exact temple plan or a prescribed ritual. Unidentified photographs remain unidentified.</p><p>Each narrative image has one visible placement. The shared site logo is repeated as branding. Glossary listening uses approximate browser speech, as labelled beside the written pronunciation hints.</p></section>
<section><h2>Suggest a correction</h2><p>A useful correction names the page, quotes the short passage in question, explains the proposed change and includes a source with an edition and chapter or verse reference. For an image, identify the subject and the specific detail that needs attention.</p><p>Send your note through <a href="/contact.html">Contact &amp; corrections</a>, or email <a href="mailto:shreembala@gmail.com">shreembala@gmail.com</a>. The <a href="https://github.com/VivekPatel-21/sanatan-heritage" rel="noopener" target="_blank">project repository on GitHub</a> also accepts contributions. Please keep private book scans and personal information out of public contributions.</p></section>
<section><h2>Your reading preferences</h2><p>Saved stories, bookmarks, reading-path completion, text size and theme preference are kept in this browser. They do not create an account or sync between devices. You can remove a story, export or import a backup, or clear reading history in your <a href="/reading-library.html">reading library</a>. <a href="/privacy.html">Reading preferences &amp; privacy</a> explains optional speech, storage and contact links.</p></section>
</div></main>
